(* q-negotiation.pvl
   The query of the control models about the Hello (AUD-5, #389; AUD-6, #409). t2 is any session of the client: what the
   query says is about the content, which a middlebox that only relays does not change. The Login of a session has one
   version, which the parser takes exactly, so it negotiates nothing, and a session negotiates its suite (q-suite.pvl). *)

(* The schema version and the Capabilities that the controller settles on for alice are ones that alice offered, so the
   attacker cannot lower them *)
(* @query negotiation *)
query t: bitstring, t2: bitstring, v: bitstring, cp: bitstring; event(ServerNegotiated(bob, alice, t, v, cp)) ==> event(ClientOffered(alice, bob, t2, v, cp)).
